course: dictionary
lesson: 15051
title: Retrieve: getting things back
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Retrieve is a verb, so it is a doing word. Its main meaning is to get something back from where it was left or lost. «I forgot my reading book, so I went back to retrieve it.» The sentence tells you that the book was left somewhere, and retrieve means fetching it back.
explain: The same idea works in other places. A computer can retrieve a file you saved last week. A dog can retrieve a ball from the grass or the water. A team can also retrieve a bad situation, which means it puts a bad moment right. Each time, something is brought back to a good state.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The team worked hard to retrieve the game after falling behind.» If you swap in "get back", the sentence still makes sense: the team got the game back into a good state. Retrieve is a useful word to know when you read about computers, dogs and sport.
fact: Retrieve means to get something back from where it was left or lost.
fact: In computing, to retrieve means to find and get back stored information, such as a file.
fact: A dog that retrieves finds something and brings it back, such as a ball or a shot bird.
fact: Golden retrievers are named for bringing things back to their owners.
fact: Only an adult should retrieve things from roads or water, because they can be dangerous.
exercise: «I forgot my reading book at school, so I went back to retrieve it.» What does retrieve mean here? | Throw it away | *To get it back | To hide it | To read it aloud
exercise: Dad says, «Our golden retriever will retrieve the ball from the pond.» Why is the dog called a retriever? | Because it only swims in the sea | Because it is very fast | *Because it finds things and brings them back | Because it likes sleeping all day
exercise: «The computer can retrieve the photo you saved last week.» What does the computer do? | Takes a brand new photo | Deletes the photo for ever | *Finds the saved photo and gets it back | Prints a copy of the screen
test: «The team worked hard to retrieve the game after falling behind.» What does retrieve mean here? | To lose the game on purpose | To run away from the game | *To put a bad situation right | To count the goals
test: Why should children ask an adult to retrieve a ball from a busy road? | Roads are too short to walk on | Adults are faster at football | *Because the road can be dangerous | Balls cannot be picked up by children
exam: «Sam searched the whole park to retrieve his lost keys.» What does retrieve mean? | To give the keys away | To buy new keys | To sell the keys | *To get back what was lost
